  "notes": "verify-B1 rerun 2026-10-25 on umbriel-b200-047 (B200, nvcc 13.4.92), rebuilt from exp/topk-swarm/B1 commit 02fdf9dbdc with --req prefer_smaller_index --control-req not_guaranteed, batch state/results/verify-B1/B1_det_vs_B1_idx_focus_v_det1_20261025_135053.json. All 28 cells within 0.3 percent (rerun vs card: fp32 N1024 k16 2137.4 vs 2138.0 against B1_idx@not_guaranteed 1794.0 vs 1794.1 = -16.1 percent both; bf16 N4096 k64 5801.1 vs 5800.8 against 3837.8 vs 3838.9 = -33.8 percent). The 8 N32768 cells come out unsupported with the IPT<=64 reason, as the card lists. Canaries 32.00098 both ends. Oracle 13/13 per cell including signed_zero exact set, variant and control. Control named and in the same lock section, not A/A. CAVEAT on the findings, not on the numbers: the commit 02fdf9dbdc source carries the 'opaque counter index' fix that the card's open question expects to remove the 344 cycles, and it was measured here against a copy with only that hunk reverted (the source as measured for the card, batch B1_det_vs_B1_idx_focus_v_det1_asmeasured_20261025_135250.json): both builds have byte-identical SASS opcode profiles (1304 instructions, 16 VOTE, 8 FLO, 8 S2R SR_LTMASK, 5 S2R SR_LANEID, 64 POPC at fp32 N1024 k16) and identical timings (2138.0 vs 2137.4 at fp32 N1024 k16). The empty asm statement on a constant does not survive ptxas, which re-derives the uniform address, so the fix as committed is a no-op and the expected gain is unsupported; either the diagnosis (aggregation at the selected-class atomic) or the fix spelling needs to change. T23's 'how to use' should say so."
